course: dictionary
lesson: 10600
title: Underwater
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Underwater means below the surface of water. The surface is the top of the water, so anything below it is underwater. «Manta rays fly through the water on wings wider than a car is long» shows animals moving below the top of the sea.
explain: Underwater can also describe something done or used under water. An «underwater camera» is made to take photos below the surface, and to «swim underwater» means to swim below the top of the water. Look for clues like water, swimming or diving around the word.
explain: Underwater can be an adjective or an adverb. As an adjective it describes a thing, as in «underwater animals». As an adverb it tells you where something happens, as in «stand on their heads underwater». To check, swap in the meaning: below the water should still make sense.
fact: Underwater means below the surface of water, or done or used under water.
fact: «A platypus closes its eyes, ears and nose underwater and finds shrimps and worms.»
fact: «Beavers can stay underwater for about 15 minutes, and see-through eyelids work like swimming goggles.»
fact: A safety rule: never push others underwater.
exercise: «The star-nosed mole smells underwater by blowing little bubbles onto things.» What does underwater mean here? | Frozen solid in ice | *Below the surface of the water | Up in the air above the trees | In a cave with no water at all
exercise: Which word in «A platypus closes its eyes, ears and nose underwater» tells you where the platypus does this? | platypus | bill | *underwater | eyes
exercise: Goggles help you see clearly when you swim. Where? | At the bus stop | *Underwater | Above the clouds | Inside a book
test: «Beavers can stay underwater for about 15 minutes.» Underwater is an adverb here. What does it mean? | Only in winter | *Below the surface of the water | On top of the water | Very fast and loud
test: Which phrase uses underwater to describe a noun? | Swim underwater | Hold your breath underwater | Push others underwater | *An underwater camera
exam: Jayden says underwater only means deep in the sea. Is he right? | Yes, only when fish are present | *No, it means below the surface of any water, like a pool or a river | No, it only means wet | Yes, only the sea counts
